    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d049222_1c4205b5",
        "filename": "common/usbc/tbt_alt_mode.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 234,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-18T20:31:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I mention elsewhere, I\u0027m not fond of the alt mode code peeking at the DPM state in this way. I think it might be better for the alt mode modules to expose to the DPM a function to indicate that exit is being requested. In this case, that function could\n1) set retry_done so that we don\u0027t try to enter again,\n2) set a flag that tbt_entry_failed (perhaps with a different name) could use to print out happy messages instead of error messages, and\n3) change the behavior of tbt_setup_next_vdm to allow starting the exit process if we\u0027re in the middle of the enter process.",
      "revId": "5c55ae120f651194718884b7fe3fd4c61b812068",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
